---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Antares Systems"
  description="How Antares Systems Ltd collects, uses and protects personal information, and your rights under UK data protection law."
  crumb="Privacy policy"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated {SITE.updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>{SITE.legalName} ("we", "us") is the controller of the personal information described in this policy. We are registered in England and Wales, company no. {SITE.companyNo}, with our registered office at {SITE.address.join(', ')}. We are registered with the Information Commissioner's Office, registration {SITE.ico}.</p>
        <p>Contact us about this policy at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enquiries.</strong> Your name, company, email address, telephone number and what you tell us in the form, by email or by phone, including the type and approximate amount of any funding you are considering.</li>
          <li><strong>Finance cases.</strong> If you ask us to prepare an introduction, further business information you choose to give us, such as company details, accounts, property or asset details, and information about directors and shareholders.</li>
          <li><strong>Website technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider processes IP addresses and basic request data to deliver and protect the site.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use analytics or advertising cookies, and the site sets no cookies that need your consent.</p>

        <h2>How and why we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to your enquiry and take steps you ask for. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests, and steps taken at your request before an agreement.</li>
          <li>To prepare your case and introduce you to our regulated partner. We do this only with your agreement.</li>
          <li>To buy and handle IT equipment you sell to us, and to keep records of those purchases.</li>
          <li>To meet legal and regulatory obligations, including record keeping and prevention of financial crime.</li>
          <li>To keep the website secure. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Our regulated partner, and lenders they approach, only after we have spoken to you and with your agreement.</li>
          <li>Service providers that help us run the business: Web3Forms (processes the enquiry form), Cloudflare (website hosting) and our email provider.</li>
          <li>Our professional advisers, and public authorities where the law requires.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>

        <h2>International transfers</h2>
        <p>Some providers process information outside the UK. Where they do, we rely on an adequacy decision or approved safeguards, such as the UK International Data Transfer Agreement or the UK Addendum to the EU standard contractual clauses.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Enquiries that do not proceed: up to 24 months.</li>
          <li>Records of introductions and equipment purchases: six years after our relationship ends, to meet legal and accounting requirements.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask us for a copy of your information, to correct it, to delete it, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to receive it in a portable format. Where we rely on your agreement, you can withdraw it at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will respond within one month.</p>
        <p>You can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113. We would welcome the chance to put things right first.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We will publish any changes to this policy on this page and update the date at the top.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
